CLI (src/cli/)
Command-line interface for interacting with Mastra agents. Built with citty.
Usage
# Run a single prompt
bun run cli agent run &lt;agentId&gt; --prompt &quot;your prompt&quot;

# Interactive chat
bun run cli agent chat &lt;agentId&gt;

# With model override
bun run cli agent chat researchAgent --model openai/gpt-4o

Available Agents



Agent ID
Description




edinburghProtocolAgent
Scottish Enlightenment reasoning


localMemoryAgent
Observational memory learning


researchAgent
Web search and calculations


weatherAgent
Weather queries



Commands
agent run
Execute a single prompt and exit.
bun run cli agent run researchAgent --prompt &quot;What&#x27;s 15% of 250?&quot;

agent chat
Start an interactive REPL session.
bun run cli agent chat researchAgent

Type exit or quit to end the session.
Structure
cli/
├── index.ts           # Entry point (citty runMain)
├── commands/
│   ├── agent.ts       # Parent command (agent run|chat)
│   ├── run.ts        # Single prompt execution
│   └── chat.ts       # Interactive REPL

Adding Commands
See citty documentation for adding new commands.
// commands/my-command.ts
import { defineCommand } from &#x27;citty&#x27;;

export const myCommand = defineCommand({
  meta: {
    name: &#x27;my-command&#x27;,
    description: &#x27;What it does&#x27;,
  },
  args: {
    input: { type: &#x27;positional&#x27;, required: true },
  },
  async run({ args }) {
    // Command logic
  },
});

Then register in index.ts:
subCommands: {
  myCommand,
}

