1887.text:
Utilities (src/utils/)
Shared utility functions used across the application.
to() - Async Result Wrapper
A strongly-typed version of await-to-js. Wraps promises to return a tuple of [error, result] instead of using try/catch.
Usage
import { to } from &#x27;@src/utils/to&#x27;;

// Instead of try/catch:
async function fetchData() {
  const [err, data] = await to(fetch(&#x27;/api/data&#x27;));

  if (err) {
    console.error(&#x27;Failed:&#x27;, err.message);
    return;
  }

  console.log(&#x27;Data:&#x27;, data);
}

// With custom error type
interface MyError {
  code: string;
}

const [err, result] = await to&lt;MyResponse, MyError&gt;(promise, { code: &#x27;CUSTOM&#x27; });

Why?

Explicit error handling: No hidden control flow
Type-safe: Full TypeScript support
Cleaner code: Avoids nested try/catch blocks
Extended errors: Add context to errors via errorExt parameter

Signature
type AsyncResult&lt;T, E = Error&gt; = Promise&lt;[E, undefined] | [null, T]&gt;;

function to&lt;T, E = Error&gt;(
  promise: Promise&lt;T&gt;, 
  errorExt?: object
): AsyncResult&lt;T, E&gt;

Adding Utilities

Create src/utils/your-util.ts
Export your functions
Import elsewhere via @src/utils/your-util

// src/utils/format.ts
export function formatDate(date: Date): string {
  return date.toISOString().split(&#x27;T&#x27;)[0];
}
